# NOTE: git has no trailing comments in .gitignore -- a '#' only starts a comment at the
# start of a line. "old_logs/  # big" matches nothing, which briefly cost 3 GB of blobs here.

# Training runs: checkpoints and tensorboard, regenerable from code + config.
# logs/shipped/ is the exception -- it is the policy the README tells you to watch, so it
# is tracked. Listing the directory rather than its contents is deliberate: git does not
# descend into an excluded directory, so `logs/` + `!logs/shipped/` would NOT work.
/logs/*
!/logs/shipped/
/.logs/

# runs/ is TRACKED, and that is the point. _write_run_manifest() writes config.json,
# command.txt, git.txt and uncommitted.patch there precisely BECAUSE logs/ is ignored --
# a few KB of text that is the only versioned record of what produced a checkpoint. This
# used to say `/runs/`, which ignored the whole thing and left every run's provenance on
# one disk: exactly the failure the manifest exists to prevent. Guard against heavy
# artifacts landing here by accident instead of ignoring the tree.
/runs/**/*.pt
/runs/**/events.out.tfevents.*

# 9.3 GB of archived training checkpoints from the development history.
old_logs/
# arduino-cli firmware build output.
build/

.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.python-version

# Local agent settings: machine-specific absolute paths, not repo content. Ignored via a
# global gitignore on the author's machine -- listed here so the protection travels.
.claude/settings.local.json

# The quickstart writes its sim rollout to ./gait.mp4, and gait_compare.mp4 is the HD
# side-by-side render kept for optional upload to GitHub's CDN. Both are regenerable, and
# neither should show up as untracked noise for anyone following the README.
gait.mp4
gait_compare.mp4

# The long-form field guide. Written, but not published yet -- it is candid about failures and
# wrong turns, and that is a deliberate decision to make once rather than by accident. Nothing
# tracked links to it, so removing this line is all it takes to ship it.
docs/detailed/

# Scratch folder of crop options for the README gif; delete once one is chosen.
gait_options/
